.\" replsh - Unified CLI for REPL servers
.TH REPLSH 1 "April 2026" "replsh" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
replsh \- unified CLI for REPL servers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B replsh
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B replsh
manages named sessions across nREPL, Python, Jupyter, and Node.js REPL servers.
It speaks each backend's native wire protocol (bencode, NDJSON/TCP, REST+WebSocket, raw TCP)
and emits structured JSON on stdout for programmatic consumption.
.PP
Built for LLMs \(em all output is machine-readable. Named sessions abstract
away connection details and persist across CLI invocations.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS launch
Spawn a REPL server process, wait for readiness, and connect.
.PP
.B replsh launch
.RI [ backend ]
.B \-\-name
.I name
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.I backend
is one of
.BR nrepl ", " python ", " jupyter ", " node .
Optional when using project config (derived from toolchain).
.TP
.BI \-\-name " name" "\fR, \fP" \-n " name"
Session name (required).
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port" "\fR, \fP" \-p " port"
Port number. If omitted, a free port is automatically allocated.
.TP
.BI \-\-cmd " command"
Shell command to spawn the REPL server.
.TP
.BI \-\-cwd " dir"
Working directory for the server process.
.TP
.BI \-\-env " K=V" "\fR, \fP" \-e " K=V"
Environment variable (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-init " code" "\fR, \fP" \-i " code"
Bootstrap code to evaluate after connecting.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " ms" "\fR, \fP" \-t " ms"
Port readiness timeout in milliseconds (default: 30000).
.TP
.BI \-\-kernel " name" "\fR, \fP" \-k " name"
Jupyter kernel name (default: python3).
.TP
.BI \-\-token " token"
Jupyter authentication token.
.TP
.BI \-\-prompt\-re " string"
Node.js prompt detection string (default: "> ").
.SS start
Connect to an already-running REPL server.
.PP
.B replsh start
.RI [ backend ]
.B \-\-name
.I name
.RI [ address ]
.PP
Same options as
.B launch
except
.B \-\-cmd
and
.BR \-\-timeout .
When not using config,
.I address
is required as
.IR host : port
(nREPL/Python/Node) or a URL (Jupyter).
.SS eval
Evaluate code in a named session. Code can be provided as a positional argument,
read from a file with
.BR \-\-file ,
or piped via stdin (when no argument or file is given).
.PP
.B replsh eval \-\-name
.I name
.RI [ code ]
.TP
.BI \-\-name " name" "\fR, \fP" \-n " name"
Session name.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " path" "\fR, \fP" \-f " path"
Read code from a file instead of a positional argument.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " ms" "\fR, \fP" \-t " ms"
Evaluation timeout in milliseconds (default: 30000).
.PP
If neither a positional argument nor
.B \-\-file
is given, code is read from standard input. This allows piping:
.PP
.nf
echo '(+ 1 2)' | replsh eval \-\-name dev
cat script.clj | replsh eval \-\-name dev
.fi
.SS ls
List all sessions.
.PP
.B replsh ls
.SS status
Show detailed status for a session including reachability and process info.
.PP
.B replsh status \-\-name
.I name
.SS stop
Stop and remove a session. Kills the server process if launched by replsh.
.PP
.B replsh stop
.I name
.SS restart
Restart a session. Re-launches the server process and re-runs init code.
.PP
.B replsh restart
.I name
.SS interrupt
Cancel a running evaluation.
.PP
.B replsh interrupt \-\-name
.I name
.SH CONFIGURATION
.SS Project config
.B .replsh/config.edn
is searched from the current working directory upward to the filesystem root.
Override with the
.B REPLSH_CONFIG
environment variable.
.PP
.nf
{:sessions
 {"backend" {:toolchain "clojure.bb"
             :port      1667
             :init      "(require '[my.app])"}}}
.fi
.PP
Session fields:
.BR :toolchain ", " :port ", " :cmd ", " :cwd ", " :init ", "
.BR :kernel ", " :token ", " :prompt\-re ", " :env .
.SS Global config
.B ~/.replsh/config.edn
defines or overrides toolchain presets. Override path with
.BR REPLSH_CONFIG_GLOBAL .
.PP
.nf
{:toolchains
 {"python.conda" {:backend  :python
                  :cmd      "conda run python {bridge} --port {port}"
                  :defaults {:port 9876}}}}
.fi
.SS Resolution order
.PP
toolchain :defaults \(-> toolchain top-level \(-> session spec \(-> CLI args
.PP
Each layer overrides the previous. CLI args always win.
.SS Template variables
Command strings support
.BR {port} ", " {cwd} ", " {host} ", and " {bridge}
placeholders, substituted at resolution time.
.B {bridge}
resolves to the path of the auto-deployed Python bridge script.
.SH TOOLCHAINS
.TS
l l l l.
Name	Backend	Default Port	Command
_
clojure.deps	nrepl	7888	clj -M:nrepl -m nrepl.cmdline --port {port}
clojure.lein	nrepl	7888	lein repl :headless :port {port}
clojure.bb	nrepl	1667	bb --nrepl-server {port}
python	python	9876	python3 {bridge} --port {port}
python.poetry	python	9876	poetry run python {bridge} --port {port}
python.venv	python	9876	{cwd}/.venv/bin/python {bridge} --port {port}
python.poetry.jupyter	jupyter	8888	poetry run jupyter server --port {port}
python.venv.jupyter	jupyter	8888	{cwd}/.venv/bin/jupyter server --port {port}
node	node	5001	node -e "require('net')..."
.TE
.SH OUTPUT FORMAT
All commands emit exactly one JSON object on stdout.
.PP
Success:
.nf
{"ok": true, "command": "eval", "data": {"value": "3", ...}}
.fi
.PP
Error:
.nf
{"ok": false, "command": "eval", "error": {"code": "eval_error", ...}}
.fi
.PP
Chunk types:
.BR out " (stdout), "
.BR err " (stderr), "
.BR value " (return value), "
.BR error " (evaluation error), "
.BR status .
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Evaluation error (code ran but produced an error).
.TP
.B 2
Client error (connection failed, session not found, bad arguments).
.TP
.B 3
Timeout.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B REPLSH_CONFIG
Override project config file path.
.TP
.B REPLSH_CONFIG_GLOBAL
Override global config file path.
.TP
.B REPLSH_STATE
Override state file path (default: ~/.replsh/state.edn).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.replsh/state.edn
Persisted session state.
.TP
.B ~/.replsh/config.edn
Global toolchain configuration.
.TP
.B ~/.replsh/logs/<name>.log
Server process stdout/stderr logs.
.TP
.B ~/.replsh/bridge/replsh_bridge.py
Python bridge script (auto-deployed).
.TP
.B <project>/.replsh/config.edn
Project session configuration.
.SH EXAMPLES
Launch from project config:
.PP
.nf
replsh launch --name backend
replsh eval --name backend '(+ 1 2)'
replsh stop backend
.fi
.PP
Launch with explicit args (port auto-allocated):
.PP
.nf
replsh launch nrepl --name dev \\
  --cmd "bb --nrepl-server {port}"
replsh launch python --name py \\
  --cmd "python3 {bridge} --port {port}"
.fi
.PP
Launch with bootstrap code:
.PP
.nf
replsh launch --name dev \\
  --init "(require '[clojure.string :as str])"
replsh eval --name dev '(str/upper-case "hello")'
.fi
.PP
Eval from file or stdin:
.PP
.nf
replsh eval --name dev --file script.clj
echo '(+ 1 2)' | replsh eval --name dev
.fi
